      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-09-22",
      "edition": "Tuesday 22 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Contract extension",
          "heading": "Sean Jansen commits to Connacht with new long-term deal until 2029",
          "body": "Ireland number eight Sean Jansen has handed Connacht a significant boost by signing a two-year contract extension, securing his future at the club until 2029. The back-rower, who made his international debut against Japan earlier this year, was voted Connacht’s Player of the Year last season after scoring 12 tries. Head coach Stuart Lancaster hailed the agreement as a “statement of intent,” noting that Jansen’s best years remain ahead of him following his impressive breakthrough into the national squad."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan defeat Fiji 20-15 to claim Pacific Nations Cup",
