          "heading": "Jordan Petaia returns to Wallabies squad following injury-plagued NFL stint",
          "body": "Utility back Jordan Petaia has been recalled to the 34-man Wallabies squad after his transition to the NFL was curtailed by a misdiagnosed hamstring injury. Petaia, who last represented Australia at the 2023 Rugby World Cup, spent four months with the Los Angeles Chargers before a tendon issue necessitated a return to rugby. Now with Japan Rugby League One side Urayasu D-Rocks, Petaia is fully focused on securing his place under head coach Les Kiss ahead of next year's home World Cup."
